From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: nadelacruz-00 <323917690+nadelacruz-00@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 22:29:43 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm: serialize devcoredump reads of the crash state

adreno_show_object() converts each captured buffer to ascii85 the first
time the crash state is shown, in place: it checks *encoded, replaces
*ptr with the encoded copy and kvfree()s the raw buffer.
msm_gpu_devcoredump_read() only takes gpu->lock around the reference
get, and every read() of the devcoredump renders the whole state again,
so two processes reading the same devcoredump at once can both see
*encoded == false and both free the same buffer, or print a buffer the
other one just freed:

  WARNING: mm/slub.c:6733 at free_large_kmalloc+0xb0/0xf8
   kvfree+0x44/0x60
   adreno_show_object+0x190/0x240
   adreno_show+0x1d0/0x438
   a6xx_show+0x68/0xbd0
   msm_gpu_devcoredump_read+0x144/0x1f8
   devcd_data_read+0x34/0x48
  page dumped because: Not a kmalloc allocation

The dump also changes length between reads, so a reader can get a
short, truncated copy that ends at a page boundary.

Seen on an Adreno 830 with IGT's msm_recovery reading the devcoredump
while a udev helper copied it out.

Add a mutex to struct msm_gpu and hold it while the state is rendered.
Only one crash state exists at a time, so a per-GPU lock is enough. It
is taken after msm_gpu_crashstate_get() and dropped before
msm_gpu_crashstate_put(), so it never nests with gpu->lock.

Signed-off-by: nadelacruz-00 <323917690+nadelacruz-00@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_gpu.c | 3 +++
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_gpu.h | 8 ++++++++
 2 files changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_gpu.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_gpu.c
index 6e326281d12..79a67e9490e 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_gpu.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_gpu.c
@@ -212,7 +212,9 @@ static ssize_t msm_gpu_devcoredump_read(char *buffer, loff_t offset,
 	if (state->cmd)
 		drm_printf(&p, "cmdline: %s\n", state->cmd);
 
+	mutex_lock(&gpu->crashstate_show_lock);
 	gpu->funcs->show(gpu, state, &p);
+	mutex_unlock(&gpu->crashstate_show_lock);
 
 	msm_gpu_crashstate_put(gpu);
 
@@ -914,6 +916,7 @@ int msm_gpu_init(struct drm_device *drm, struct platform_device *pdev,
 	gpu->funcs = funcs;
 	gpu->name = name;
 	INIT_WORK(&gpu->crashstate_free_work, msm_gpu_crashstate_free_worker);
+	mutex_init(&gpu->crashstate_show_lock);
 
 	gpu->worker = kthread_run_worker(0, "gpu-worker");
 	if (IS_ERR(gpu->worker)) {
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_gpu.h b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_gpu.h
index 68a89e4e819..5f61fd61a6b 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_gpu.h
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_gpu.h
@@ -264,6 +264,14 @@ struct msm_gpu {
 	 */
 	struct work_struct crashstate_free_work;
 
+	/**
+	 * @crashstate_show_lock: serializes rendering of @crashstate for the
+	 * devcoredump.  The show functions convert captured buffers to ascii85
+	 * in place on first use (see adreno_show_object()), so concurrent
+	 * readers of the same dump must not render it at the same time.
+	 */
+	struct mutex crashstate_show_lock;
+
 	/**
 	 * @recovery_in_progress: set by recover_worker() under @lock, so that
 	 * fault capture and GMU waits don't wait on a fault devcoredump that
